comments.body:
@aloisklink why don't we lock the package versions of `mermaid` & `@mermaid-js/examples`?

I've done it for the `@mermaid-js/tiny` package in https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid/pull/4734, we can use the same approach here as well. 

Unlike `@mermaid-js/tiny`, there will be some unnecessary releases in `@mermaid-js/examples`, but it'll make the UX much easier, as it's clear that the examples for `mermaid@x.y.z` will be in `@mermaid-js/examples@x.y.z`.
